  "slides": [
    {"content":"<h1>How to Pass Creación Digital I</h1><h2>Universidad Europea · UEM 2026-27</h2><p><strong>Rubén Vega Balbás, PhD</strong></p><p><em>6 ECTS · 150 h · 80 h contact</em></p><p>Final event theme: <strong>Communicate and inspire: What is fashion for you?</strong></p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Official weights (unchanged)</h2><p>Follow the UEM guía table for this subject (knowledge / case / projects / notebook). Studio choreography below maps onto those instruments — it does not rewrite them.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Every session (order binding)</h2><ol><li><strong>Analysis strip</strong> — sessions 1–2: professor models analysis; from session 3: <strong>2 students × 15 min</strong> defence</li><li><strong>Masterclass</strong> — ideas + images</li><li><strong>Lab (Portfolio)</strong> — exercises + debates → portfolio</li><li><strong>Workshop (Deliverable)</strong> — time on the next graded deliverable</li></ol><p><em>Lab ≠ Workshop.</em> Lab leaves traces; Workshop advances deliverables. Names are not swapped.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Slide rule</h2><p>Before Lab exercises, a <strong>geometrical</strong> slide announces: exercises are coming and they go into your <strong>portfolio index</strong>.</p><p>Workshop open + outro also use geometrical backgrounds. Masterclass content uses accepted course media packs.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Five deliverables</h2><ol><li><strong>D1 Analysis</strong> — 15 min defence · slideshow · fashion image related to a <strong>Madrid exhibition</strong> piece (coordinated visit)</li><li><strong>D2 Transposition</strong> — critical review / palimpsest · output <strong>into an image</strong></li><li><strong>D3 Atrium</strong> — tech script + live defence · <em>What is fashion for you?</em></li><li><strong>D4 Portfolio index</strong> — Lab exercises + D1–D3</li><li><strong>D5 Exam</strong> — test/questionnaire + final self-review of process</li></ol>"},
    {"content":"<h2>D1 intra-rubric</h2><table><tr><th>Presentation</th><td>70%</td></tr><tr><th>Deliverable support</th><td>20%</td></tr><tr><th>Peer debate</th><td>10%</td></tr></table><p>Two students per session from session 3. Source files + process trail required.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Ordinary / extraordinary</h2><p>Binding dates: official UEM guide + Campus Virtual. Teaching evidence is not research data — exhibition needs consent.</p>","calendar_note":true},
    {"content":"<h2>Next step</h2><p>Start the portfolio index now. Prepare D1 around the Madrid visit brief. Ask before publishing student work.</p>"}
